            4. Banana Protein Powder vs Adding a Real Banana
          </h2>

          <p>
            A medium banana adds roughly 105 calories, 27 g of carbohydrate, about 14 g of natural sugar, 3 g of fiber and around 420 mg of potassium, per USDA data. Blended into a shake, it also adds body and natural sweetness, so you can use an unflavored or lightly sweetened protein and still get a drink that tastes like dessert.
          </p>

